%U A402447 4,2,6,0,8,8,2,9,5,9,6,6,9,7,3,8,5,7,3,6,0,2,0,3,9,6,3,4,0,6,1,4
%N A402447 Decimal expansion of the limit of the proportion of steps at which a card is read for the first time in the deck process of A402446.
%C A402447 A402446(n) is the label of the card read at step n of the following process. Start with an infinite deck of cards labeled 1, 2, 3, ..., with card 1 on top. At step n = 1, 2, 3, ..., read the top card, remove it, and put it back so that exactly 2*(n - k) of the remaining cards are above it, where k is the last earlier step at which this card was read (k = 0 if it was not read before). Let K(t) be the number of distinct cards read in the first t steps, so that K(t)/t is the proportion of these steps at which a card is read for the first time. It is proved in the notes file of A402446, with computer assistance, that K(t)/t converges as t -> oo; its limit is the constant alpha of this entry.
%C A402447 For real x >= 0 let H_0(x) = 0, H_1(x) = x and H_(r+1)(x) = H_r(x)*(1 + H_r(x) - H_(r-1)(x)) for r >= 1, so H_2(x) = x + x^2 and H_3(x) = x + x^2 + x^3 + x^4. For each m >= 0 the coefficient of x^m in H_r(x) becomes constant as r grows; these constants are A045761(m), and the values H_r(1) are A001696(r). Since H_(r+1)(x) - H_r(x) = H_r(x)*(H_r(x) - H_(r-1)(x)), the numbers H_r(x) do not decrease as r grows; let H(x) be their limit, which may be infinite. Equivalently, H(x) = Sum_{m>=1} A045761(m)*x^m.
%C A402447 For r >= 1 the proportion of the first t steps at which a card is read for the r-th time tends to b_r = 2*(H_r(alpha/2) - H_(r-1)(alpha/2)), so b_1 = alpha, b_(r+1) = b_r*(b_1 + ... + b_r)/2 and Sum_{r>=1} b_r = 2*H(alpha/2) = 1 (proved with computer assistance in the notes file of A402446).
%C A402447 The function H has a threshold lambda: H(x) < 1 for 0 <= x < lambda, H(lambda) = 1, and H(x) is infinite for x > lambda, so lambda is the only x > 0 with H(x) = 1 (proved without computation). This threshold lambda = 0.39952466709... is the constant of A268107. For the deck of A402125 (put back below n - k cards instead of 2*(n - k)), with K(t) defined in the same way, it is proved there that liminf K(t)/t <= lambda <= limsup K(t)/t; convergence is conjectured. See the notes file of A402446 in the Links section for proofs, sources and further data.
%H A402447 Alper Ferudun, <a href="/A402446/a402446.txt">Notes, proofs and sources</a> (for A402446).
%F A402447 alpha = 2*x_0, where x_0 = 0.3181256990875532789... is the only x > 0 with H(x) = 1/2 (proved with computer assistance in the notes file of A402446).
%e A402447 0.636251398175106557859945417464698215503919619700...
%e A402447 The first ten steps of A402446 read the cards 1, 2, 3, 1, 4, 5, 2, 6, 7, 3. At step 1, card 1 (k = 0) goes below 2 cards, giving the deck 2, 3, 1, 4, 5, ...; steps 2 and 3 move cards 2 and 3 behind it, so it is read again at step 4 (k = 1) and then goes below 2*(4 - 1) = 6 cards. Cards are read for the first time at steps 1, 2, 3, 5, 6, 8, 9, so K(10) = 7.
%e A402447 The values K(10^m) for m = 0, ..., 9 are 1, 7, 65, 637, 6363, 63629, 636258, 6362538, 63625171, 636251475; thus K(10^9)/10^9 = 0.636251475.
%o A402447 (Python)
%o A402447 d = 100; Q = 10**(d + 40)
%o A402447 def bounds(x):
%o A402447     b0 = h0 = x//2
%o A402447     b1 = h1 = (x + 1)//2
%o A402447     for _ in range(499):
%o A402447         b0, b1 = b0*h0//Q, (b1*h1 + Q - 1)//Q
%o A402447         h0, h1 = h0 + b0, h1 + b1
%o A402447     upper = h1 + 4*((b1*h1 + Q - 1)//Q)
%o A402447     assert 4*upper < 3*Q
%o A402447     return h0, upper
%o A402447 lo, hi = 635*Q//1000, 638*Q//1000
%o A402447 assert 2*bounds(lo)[1] < Q < 2*bounds(hi)[0]
%o A402447 while lo//10**40 != hi//10**40:
%o A402447     m = (lo + hi)//2; lower, upper = bounds(m)
%o A402447     if 2*upper < Q: lo = m
%o A402447     elif 2*lower > Q: hi = m
%o A402447     else: raise ArithmeticError("Increase precision")
%o A402447 print(*str(lo//10**40).zfill(d), sep=",")
%Y A402447 Cf. A001696, A045761, A268107, A402125, A402446.
%K A402447 nonn,cons,new
%O A402447 0,1
